<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Arianiti</h1><p class="st-meta">1432 CE – 1462 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lands of the Albanian lord Gjergj Arianiti, who led an early revolt against the Ottomans and became Skanderbeg's ally and father-in-law.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Arianiti were an old noble family of central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>, holding lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkumbin">Shkumbin</a> valley and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbasan">Elbasan</a>. In 1432 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjergj-arianiti">Gjergj Arianiti</a>, who had been a hostage at the Ottoman court, led a rising against the new Ottoman land registers and defeated several Ottoman armies in the mountains between 1432 and 1436.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of how the lands were governed: they were a mountain lordship of fortified villages and clan levies rather than a state with fixed institutions, and no clear capital is recorded. Gjergj built ties through marriage, wedding his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donika-kastrioti">Donika</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> in 1451, and negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjergj-arianiti">Gjergj Arianiti</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a> in 1444, though he later quarrelled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>. He died in 1462, and the family's lands fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the following years. His descendants, the Arianiti Comneni, settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1432 CE – 1462 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.20%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1432 CE – 1462 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gjergj Arianiti</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arianiti lands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1447&amp;focus=principality-of-arianiti" aria-label="Principality of Arianiti on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5169 729 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Arianiti lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5478 945h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5489 985h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5489 985h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Albania. <a href="/atlas?year=1447&amp;focus=principality-of-arianiti">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

